<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antipope Anacletus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 1138</span> · Also known as Pietro Pierleoni</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anacletus II, born Pietro Pierleoni, was an antipope from 1130 to 1138. Elected by a majority of the cardinals in a disputed election against Innocent II, he held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> but was rejected by most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernard-of-clairvaux">Bernard of Clairvaux</a>. In return for his support he granted Roger II a royal title in 1130, founding the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>.</p></div>
